// title: List all the vulnerabilities each device has in a pivot table · Defender XDR
// date: 2026-10-21
// product: Defender for Endpoint
// tables: DeviceTvmSoftwareVulnerabilities
// purpose: This query returns a row for each device with the amount of Critical, High, Medium and Low Vulnerabilities that device has.
// source: https://github.com/Bert-JanP/Hunting-Queries-Detection-Rules/blob/65d11700e1cb878403d87312acdd6b9a8dd622c1/Vulnerability%20Management/Pivot%20-%20DeviceVulnerabilities.md
// kind: repo
// author: Bert-Jan Pals
// license: BSD-3-Clause (as stated by the repository)
// archived by tools/kql_archive.py (CLAUDE.md 5l, 5eu)
DeviceTvmSoftwareVulnerabilities
| project DeviceName, VulnerabilitySeverityLevel
| evaluate pivot(VulnerabilitySeverityLevel): (DeviceName: string,Critical: long, High: long, Medium: long, Low: long)
| sort by Critical, High, Medium, Low
